    Check if a public key has permission to perform an action.BUG FIX: this method was expected to exist by ContextBase (which alreadychecked `typeof this.#roleBase.can === 'function'` and called it formoderation permission checks), but was never actually added — meaningthat check always silently failed and moderation events were alwaysqueued as pending rather than actually evaluated against the registry,even when a RoleBase was properly attached. The standalone `can()`function this wraps was already imported and used internally in thisfile for role-modification checks; it just wasn't exposed for externalcallers.
</div>









