    <h4 class="name" id="refusal"><span class="type-signature">(async) </span>refusal<span class="signature">()</span><span class="type-signature"> &rarr; {Promise.&lt;(string|null)>}</span></h4>
    

    



<div class="description">
    Why this peer can't apply this context, if that is already known locally:it was interrupted, or the context's record is held locally and refusesthis peer's rules or version. Never waits on the network — a fresh peerthat hasn't received the record yet finds out when it applies.
</div>













<dl class="details">

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    

    
