    <h4 class="name" id="withWriteLock"><span class="type-signature">(async) </span>withWriteLock<span class="signature">(fn)</span><span class="type-signature"> &rarr; {Promise.&lt;*>}</span></h4>
    

    



<div class="description">
    Run `fn(length)` while holding this core's write lock. `length` is wherethe next appended block will land, and stays true for as long as `fn`runs — which is what lets a caller build events that embed their ownfuture seq (a bulk write's entity ids) before appending them. Inside`fn`, append with UserCore#appendBatchUnlocked; the lockedmethods would wait on the lock `fn` itself holds.
</div>









